/*
Problem: 3Sum Closest
Platform: LeetCode
Difficulty: Medium
Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/3sum-closest/

Approach:
First, sort the array.

Use a for loop to fix one number, nums[i].
Then use two pointers:
- left = i + 1
- right = n - 1

Calculate the sum of these three numbers.

If the current sum is closer to the target than our previous
closest sum, update closest.

Then:
- If sum < target, move left forward because we need a bigger sum.
- If sum > target, move right backward because we need a smaller sum.
- If sum == target, return immediately because this is the exact answer.

The for loop is used to choose the first number of the triplet.
For every fixed nums[i], the two pointers find the best possible
pair from the remaining part of the sorted array.

Time Complexity: O(n^2)
Space Complexity: O(1) extra space
(ignoring the space used internally by sort)

Important Tip:
Whenever the array is sorted and we need to find a combination
of numbers close to a target, think about Two Pointers.

The key movement rule is:

sum < target  -> left++
sum > target  -> right--
sum == target -> exact answer

Mistake I Made:
I need to carefully understand the role of the for loop.

The for loop does NOT directly find the answer.
It fixes the first element of the triplet.

Example:
i = 0  -> nums[i] is the first number
i = 1  -> nums[i] is the first number
i = 2  -> nums[i] is the first number
...

For every i, the left and right pointers search for the other
two numbers.

Important Learning:
Sorting allows us to decide which pointer to move.

If the sum is too small, moving left forward increases the sum.
If the sum is too large, moving right backward decreases the sum.

Pattern:
Sort + Fix One Element + Two Pointers = 3Sum pattern
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int threeSumClosest(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int n = nums.size();

        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        int closest = nums[0] + nums[1] + nums[2];

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {
            int left = i + 1;
            int right = n - 1;

            while (left < right) {
                int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];

                if (abs(sum - target) < abs(closest - target)) {
                    closest = sum;
                }

                if (sum < target) {
                    left++;
                }
                else if (sum > target) {
                    right--;
                }
                else {
                    return sum;
                }
            }
        }

        return closest;
    }
};
